    c2:bc_definition "A standardized clinical tool, published in 1980 by Harvey et al. as a simplified version of the Crohn Disease Activity Index (CDAI), that assesses and scores five patient parameters (well-being, abdominal pain, number of liquid or soft stools, abdominal mass, and complications) to stratify Crohn's disease severity." ;
    c2:bc_hierarchy_full "Clinical or Research Assessment Classification (C118969); Harvey-Bradshaw Index Clinical Classification (C191036)" ;
