    c2:bc_definition "A measurement of the clotting time of plasma recalcified in the presence of excess tissue thromboplastin; it is a measure of the extrinsic pathway of coagulation. It is used to determine the clotting tendency of blood, in the measure of warfarin dosage, liver damage and vitamin K status. Factors measured are fibrinogen, prothrombin, and factors V, VII, and X." ;
    c2:bc_hierarchy_full "Prothrombin Activity Measurement (C98774); Prothrombin Time (C62656)" ;
