    c1:definition "An assessment performed to estimate peripheral perfusion and hydration status. The test is most often conducted by applying constant manual pressure for a set time on a patient's nail bed and then releasing while observing the length of time it takes for color to return to the tissue. A prolonged return to baseline coloring may indicate compromise of peripheral blood flow." ;
    c1:ncit_code "C168125" ;
    c1:ncit_dec_code "C70856" ;
    c1:package_date "2026-03-31" ;
    c1:parent_bc_id "C122008" ;
    c1:result_scales "Quantitative" ;
    c1:short_name "Capillary Refill Test" ;
    c1:synonyms "Capillary Refill Time;CPLRFLT" ;
    c1:system "http://loinc.org/" ;
    c1:system_name "LOINC" ;
.

